bt_ebitda":null,"_gate_accruals":-0.0342261590791572,"_gp_accruals":true,"_score_accruals":77.3,"_gate_rev_volatility":0.12623787597923597,"_gp_rev_volatility":false,"_score_rev_volatility":78.2,"_gate_margin_vs_hist":0.036880225759251234,"_gp_margin_vs_hist":true,"_score_margin_vs_hist":53.9,"_gate_piotroski":4,"_gp_piotroski":false,"_score_piotroski":44.4,"_gate_spread":null,"_gp_spread":null,"_score_spread":null,"_gate_roic_consistency":null,"_gp_roic_consistency":null,"_score_roic_consistency":null,"_gate_incr_roic":null,"_gp_incr_roic":null,"_score_incr_roic":null,"_gate_margin_advantage":null,"_gp_margin_advantage":null,"_score_margin_advantage":null,"_gate_pool_share":0.08181789968878417,"_gp_pool_share":true,"_score_pool_share":72.7,"_gate_rev_durability":0.09007300440447419,"_gp_rev_durability":true,"_score_rev_durability":70.0,"_gate_fcf_durability":null,"_gp_fcf_durability":null,"_score_fcf_durability":null,"_gate_margins":null,"_gp_margins":null,"_score_margins":null,"_gate_fund_growth":null,"_gp_fund_growth":null,"_score_fund_growth":null,"_gate_shrhldr_yield":0.03779137730438509,"_gp_shrhldr_yield":true,"_score_shrhldr_yield":53.1,"_gate_share_shrink":0.0025337710290673776,"_gp_share_shrink":false,"_score_share_shrink":46.8,"_gate_sbc_dilution":null,"_gp_sbc_dilution":null,"_score_sbc_dilution":0.0,"_gate_insider_own":0.01602,"_gp_insider_own":false,"_score_insider_own":10.7,"_gate_insider_buying":null,"_gp_insider_buying":null,"_score_insider_buying":null,"pf":[],"description_full":"RLI Corp., an insurance holding company, provides property, casualty, and surety insurance products. Its Casualty segment provides commercial excess, personal umbrella, general liability, transportation, and management liability coverages; professional liability and workers' compensation for office-based professional coverages; commercial automobile liability and physical damage insurance to local, intermediate and long haul truckers, public transportation entities, and other specialty commercial automobile risks; incidental related insurance coverages; inland marine coverages; directors and officers liability insurance, fiduciary liability and coverages, employment practice liability, public and private businesses risk, and home business insurance products. This segment also offers coverages for security guards and environmental liability for underground storage tanks, contractors and asbestos, and environmental remediation specialists; and professional liability coverages for errors and omission coverage for small to medium-sized design, technical, computer, and miscellaneous professionals. The company's Property segment offers commercial property insurance, such as fire, wind, difference in conditions, earthquake, flood, and collapse coverages; insurance for office buildings, apartments, condominiums, and industrial and mercantile structures; and cargo, hull, protection and indemnity, marine liability, inland marine, homeowners' and dwelling fire, and other property insurance products. Its Surety segment provides commercial surety bonds for medium and large-sized businesses; small bonds for businesses and individuals; and bonds for small to medium-sized contractors. The company offers reinsurance coverages. It markets its products through branch offices, wholesale and retail brokers, carrier partners, and underwriting and independent agents. RLI Corp. was incorporated in 1965 and is headquartered in Peoria, Illinois.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Craig William Kliethermes CPCU, FCAS, MAAA | President, CEO & Director | Age 60 | Compensation: $6.9M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 1K people. Revenue per employee of $1.6M ranks in the top quartile among Financial Services peers, with revenue growing 8%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $510K of free cash flow annually. CEO compensation is 4\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags low compensation governance risk (1/10).","financial_summary":["RLI Corp. is a mid-cap financial services business with a $6.4B market cap on $1.9B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +3% over the past three years and +9% annually across the full decade, which puts it in mature, slow-growth territory.","Returns on capital run at 24% against a 7% cost of capital \u2014 a 17-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat.","The business throws off $609M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 32 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders, and cash conversion sits at 1.52\u00d7 so those profits are backed by real cash.","On the balance sheet, leverage is comfortably conservative at 0.0\u00d7 net debt/EBITDA, and interest coverage of 95\u00d7 is fortress-like.","Shareholder yield of 3.8% reflects a genuine commitment to returning capital rather than empire-building, and insider ownership is negligible, so management has little personal stake in the long-term outcome."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Low reinvestment-driven growth suggests the compounding engine has stalled","sev":"amber","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Trading near 52-week highs \u2014 the market has already recognised the story (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"amber","cat":"valuation","magnitude":0.39123376623376677},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Piotroski score 4/9 \u2014 below the median for a healthy business","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Altman Z in the grey zone \u2014 financial health warrants monitoring","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Credit cycles and regulatory capital \u2014 losses accumulate invisibly in good years and appear all at once, and the time to worry is when underwriting standards are loosest.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Fintech disintermediation \u2014 neobanks, embedded finance, and blockchain rails are unbundling the fee streams that traditional banks took for granted.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"},{"text":"Interest rate regime shifts \u2014 a rapid move in rates can invert the yield curve, crush bond portfolios, and trigger deposit flight simultaneously.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["38 consecutive years of dividend payments \u2014 an operating record that makes the dividend claim credible","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment","Minimal goodwill on the balance sheet \u2014 low impairment risk"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"RLI (RLI) Could Be 19% Overvalued As Special Dividend Draws Attention","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-rli/rli/news/rli-rli-could-be-19-overvalued-as-special-dividend-draws-att","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794594167.944,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.969,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"How Investors Are Reacting To RLI (RLI) Special Dividend Declaration","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/insurance/nyse-rli/rli/news/how-investors-are-reacting-to-rli-rli-special-dividend-decla","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794504094.094,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.954,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["dividend"]},{"title":"RLI Corp. Announces $3.00 Special Dividend Alongside $0.18 Quarterly Dividend for December 2026","source":"kalkinemedia.com","link":"https://kalkinemedia.com/us/news/announcements/rli-corp-announces-300-special-dividend-alongside-018-quarterly-dividend-for-december-2026","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482881.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.402,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["earnings","dividend"]},{"title":"RLI declares $0.18 dividend & special cash dividend of $3.00/share (NYSE:RL